  2	// only). Unlike the read-only web-research tools (web-tools.ts), this one is
  3	// bound to a specific campaign/JD per request via makeSourcingToolRunner() and
  4	// accumulates every REAL candidate it finds — the caller reads that
  5	// accumulated list after the loop finishes instead of trusting the model to
  6	// echo back names/scores/URLs correctly in its final text.
  7	//
  8	// search_candidates reuses the exact real-sourcing pipeline already shipped:
  9	// GitHub's Search API (keyless by default) for GitHub, and the compliant
 10	// web_search tool (site:-scoped) + extractLead for LinkedIn/Stack Overflow/
 11	// Dribbble/Behance — the SAME mapGithubCandidates/mapWebSearchCandidates that
 12	// already do real dedupe + real deterministic scoring. The model never invents
 13	// a candidate or a score; it only chooses which real, already-scored people to
 14	// draft outreach for.
